The next trade-off after filtering for foods eaten in one
turn is nutrition-to-weight ratio and total nutrition.  A
meatball only takes one turn to eat and it weighs
little but its nutrition is too small to bother with.  An
egg a 80 and a lump of royal jelly at 100 are very
good for the weight, K-rations at 400 are very good for
the nutrition.

I tend to hoard all K-rations and C-rations in the game
for the astral level, eat all royal jelly immediately for the
strength.  I wonder if the hunger damage done by
Famine is small enough to justify the 100 nutrition
points of royal jelly?  Whack him until he dies, eat a
couple of K-rations, resume the run towards the nearest
high altar - Not sure it that's the best strategy when
facing him.


